OL,3,AUN warns of 'supersized' El Nino as
OL,4,Acountries prepare for impact
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe world has entered a "danger zone of
OL,7,Fextreme weather" as the impacts of El
OL,8,FNino start to be felt globally, UN head
OL,9,FAntonio Guterres has warned.
OL,11,FThe World Meteorological Organization
OL,12,F(WMO) has released the latest data on
OL,13,Fthe natural weather phenomenon showing
OL,14,Fit could be the strongest for more than
OL,15,F70 years and last until at least
OL,16,FFebruary 2027.
OL,18,FEl Nino changes weather patterns around
OL,19,Fthe world, pushing some regions into
OL,20,Fdrought whilst others experience
OL,21,Fstronger typhoons and flooding.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,0,100
